# BEGIN 12id DOCKER-USER
# Appended to /etc/ufw/after.rules on the staging VM.
#
# Docker-published ports bypass ufw, so ufw's own rules cannot close them. von-network
# publishes its node-to-node consensus ports (9701/9703/9705/9707) on all interfaces.
# The nodes must reach each other through the public IP, because that is the address in
# the genesis. That traffic leaves via ens3, hairpins through the provider's 1:1 NAT, and
# comes back in on ens3 with source 10.1.1.1 (the provider gateway, observed with tcpdump).
# Allow that; drop everyone else. Internet traffic keeps its real source address, so this
# does not open the ports publicly (verified from outside).
# Client ports (9702/9704/9706/9708) stay public on purpose: phones read the ledger there.
#
# Matching on --ctorigdstport keeps the rule correct after Docker's DNAT.
*filter
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i ens3 -s 10.1.1.1/32 -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i ens3 -p tcp -m conntrack --ctorigdstport 9701 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i ens3 -p tcp -m conntrack --ctorigdstport 9703 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i ens3 -p tcp -m conntrack --ctorigdstport 9705 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -i ens3 -p tcp -m conntrack --ctorigdstport 9707 -j DROP
-A DOCKER-USER -j RETURN
COMMIT
# END 12id DOCKER-USER
